<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Extending Section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 A new interpretation: REINFORCE is inherently off-policy ‣ 2 Two interpretations for REINFORCE ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> to multi-step RL</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section extends the off-policy interpretation proposed in Section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 A new interpretation: REINFORCE is inherently off-policy ‣ 2 Two interpretations for REINFORCE ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> to multi-step RL settings.
Let us start by introducing some notations.
In multi-step RL, the initial prompt <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is also regarded as the initial state <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{1}=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{1}=x</annotation></semantics></math>.
A rollout trajectory consisting of multiple turns of agent-environment interaction is denoted by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}=(s^{1},a^{1},s^{2},a^{2},\dots)=(s^{\ell},a^{\ell})_{1\leq\ell\leq|\mathcal{T}|}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}=(s^{1},a^{1},s^{2},a^{2},\dots)=(s^{\ell},a^{\ell})_{1\leq\ell\leq|\mathcal{T}|},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is the state and <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is the action, i.e., an LLM response (akin to <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> in Section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 A new interpretation: REINFORCE is inherently off-policy ‣ 2 Two interpretations for REINFORCE ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>).
Let <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the context up to step <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>,
so that <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a^{\ell}\sim\pi(\cdot|c^{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\ell}\sim\pi(\cdot|c^{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> for some policy <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.
Throughout this section, we consider trajectory-level rewards <math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,\mathcal{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,\mathcal{T})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A1.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\rho_{\bm{\theta}}(\cdot|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\bm{\theta}}(\cdot|x)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the trajectory distribution induced by policy <math id="A1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\bm{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\bm{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> at initial state <math id="A1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{1}=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{1}=x</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The following analysis focuses on the <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th iteration,
updating the policy model from <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\theta}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\theta}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\theta}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\theta}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: surrogate objective and consistency condition.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th iteration of policy optimization, consider the following KL-regularized objective:</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\max_{\bm{\theta}}\quad J(\bm{\theta};\pi_{\bm{\theta}_{t}})\coloneqq{\mathbb{E}}_{x\sim D}\bigg[{\mathbb{E}}_{\mathcal{T}\sim\rho_{\bm{\theta}}(\cdot|x)}[r(x,\mathcal{T})]-\tau\cdot D_{\textsf{KL}}\big(\rho_{\bm{\theta}}(\cdot|x)\,\|\,\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\cdot|x)\big)\bigg]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></munder><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\bm{\theta}}\quad J(\bm{\theta};\pi_{\bm{\theta}_{t}})\coloneqq{\mathbb{E}}_{x\sim D}\bigg[{\mathbb{E}}_{\mathcal{T}\sim\rho_{\bm{\theta}}(\cdot|x)}[r(x,\mathcal{T})]-\tau\cdot D_{\textsf{KL}}\big(\rho_{\bm{\theta}}(\cdot|x)\,\|\,\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\cdot|x)\big)\bigg].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The optimal policy <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and the induced trajectory distribution <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the following:
for any trajectory <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho(\mathcal{T}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho(\mathcal{T}|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\mathcal{T}|x)e^{r(x,\mathcal{T})/\tau}}{Z(x,\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}})},\quad\text{where}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\mathcal{T}|x)e^{r(x,\mathcal{T})/\tau}}{Z(x,\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}})},\quad\text{where}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z(x,\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z(x,\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\int\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\mathcal{T}^{\prime}|x)e^{r(x,\mathcal{T}^{\prime})/\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathcal{T}^{\prime}={\mathbb{E}}_{\mathcal{T}^{\prime}\sim\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\cdot|x)}[e^{r(x,\mathcal{T}^{\prime})/\tau}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\int\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\mathcal{T}^{\prime}|x)e^{r(x,\mathcal{T}^{\prime})/\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathcal{T}^{\prime}={\mathbb{E}}_{\mathcal{T}^{\prime}\sim\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\cdot|x)}[e^{r(x,\mathcal{T}^{\prime})/\tau}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This is equivalent to the following: for any pair of trajectories <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\rho(\mathcal{T}_{1}|x)}{\rho(\mathcal{T}_{2}|x)}=\frac{\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\mathcal{T}_{1}|x)}{\pi_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\mathcal{T}_{2}|x)}e^{\big(r(x,\mathcal{T}_{1})-r(x,\mathcal{T}_{2})\big)/\tau}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\rho(\mathcal{T}_{1}|x)}{\rho(\mathcal{T}_{2}|x)}=\frac{\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\mathcal{T}_{1}|x)}{\pi_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\mathcal{T}_{2}|x)}e^{\big(r(x,\mathcal{T}_{1})-r(x,\mathcal{T}_{2})\big)/\tau}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Taking logarithm of both sides and doing some rearrangement, we have equivalently</p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r(x,\mathcal{T}_{1})-\tau\cdot\big(\log\rho(\mathcal{T}_{1}|x)-\log\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\mathcal{T}_{1}|x)\big)=r(x,\mathcal{T}_{2})-\tau\cdot\big(\log\rho(\mathcal{T}_{2}|x)-\log\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\mathcal{T}_{2}|x)\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r(x,\mathcal{T}_{1})-\tau\cdot\big(\log\rho(\mathcal{T}_{1}|x)-\log\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\mathcal{T}_{1}|x)\big)=r(x,\mathcal{T}_{2})-\tau\cdot\big(\log\rho(\mathcal{T}_{2}|x)-\log\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\mathcal{T}_{2}|x)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Note that for a trajectory <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\rho(\mathcal{T}|x)-\log\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\mathcal{T}|x)=\sum_{\ell}\log\pi(a^{\ell}|c^{\ell})-\sum_{\ell}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(a^{\ell}|c^{\ell})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\rho(\mathcal{T}|x)-\log\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\mathcal{T}|x)=\sum_{\ell}\log\pi(a^{\ell}|c^{\ell})-\sum_{\ell}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(a^{\ell}|c^{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">since the state-transition probability terms in <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\rho(\mathcal{T}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\rho(\mathcal{T}|x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\mathcal{T}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\rho_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(\mathcal{T}|x)</annotation></semantics></math> cancel out.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: surrogate loss with finite samples.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories from the same initial state <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}=x</annotation></semantics></math>,
we define the following mean-squared surrogate loss that enforces the consistency condition:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{L}({\bm{\theta}};x,\pi_{\bm{\theta}_{t}})\coloneqq\frac{1}{K^{2}}\sum_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq K}\frac{(a_{i}-a_{j})^{2}}{(1+\tau)^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{L}({\bm{\theta}};x,\pi_{\bm{\theta}_{t}})\coloneqq\frac{1}{K^{2}}\sum_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq K}\frac{(a_{i}-a_{j})^{2}}{(1+\tau)^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{where}\quad a_{i}\coloneqq r(x,\mathcal{T}_{i})-\tau\Big(\sum_{\ell}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a^{\ell}_{i}|c^{\ell}_{i})-\sum_{\ell}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(a^{\ell}_{i}|c^{\ell}_{i})\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{where}\quad a_{i}\coloneqq r(x,\mathcal{T}_{i})-\tau\Big(\sum_{\ell}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a^{\ell}_{i}|c^{\ell}_{i})-\sum_{\ell}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}(a^{\ell}_{i}|c^{\ell}_{i})\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">With infinite samples and sufficient coverage of the action space, the optimum of this surrogate loss would be the same as the optimal policy for the surrogate objective in Eq. (<a href="#A1.E11" title="In Step 1: surrogate objective and consistency condition. ‣ Appendix A Extending Section to multi-step RL ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 3: one gradient step of the surrogate loss.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By the same trick as in Section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 A new interpretation: REINFORCE is inherently off-policy ‣ 2 Two interpretations for REINFORCE ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}{(a_{i}-a_{j})^{2}}\big|_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}={-2\tau}\,\Big(r(x,\mathcal{T}_{i})-r(x,\mathcal{T}_{j})\Big)\Big(\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\sum_{\ell}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a^{\ell}_{i}|c^{\ell}_{i})\big|_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}-\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\sum_{\ell}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a^{\ell}_{j}|c^{\ell}_{j})\big|_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}\Big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}{(a_{i}-a_{j})^{2}}\big|_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}={-2\tau}\,\Big(r(x,\mathcal{T}_{i})-r(x,\mathcal{T}_{j})\Big)\Big(\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\sum_{\ell}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a^{\ell}_{i}|c^{\ell}_{i})\big|_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}-\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\sum_{\ell}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a^{\ell}_{j}|c^{\ell}_{j})\big|_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\sum_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq K}\frac{(a_{i}-a_{j})^{2}}{(1+\tau)^{2}}\Big|_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}=\frac{-2\tau K}{(1+\tau)^{2}}\sum_{1\leq i\leq K}\big(r(x,\mathcal{T}_{i})-\overline{r}(x)\big)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\sum_{\ell}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a^{\ell}_{i}|c^{\ell}_{i})\Big|_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\sum_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq K}\frac{(a_{i}-a_{j})^{2}}{(1+\tau)^{2}}\Big|_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}=\frac{-2\tau K}{(1+\tau)^{2}}\sum_{1\leq i\leq K}\big(r(x,\mathcal{T}_{i})-\overline{r}(x)\big)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\sum_{\ell}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a^{\ell}_{i}|c^{\ell}_{i})\Big|_{\bm{\theta}_{t}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{r}(x)\coloneqq\sum_{1\leq j\leq K}r(x,\mathcal{T}_{j})/K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{r}(x)\coloneqq\sum_{1\leq j\leq K}r(x,\mathcal{T}_{j})/K</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the group mean reward in the last line.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In sum, the gradient of the surrogate loss in Eq. (<a href="#A1.E16" title="In Step 2: surrogate loss with finite samples. ‣ Appendix A Extending Section to multi-step RL ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) becomes:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\widehat{L}(\bm{\theta};x,\pi_{\bm{\theta}_{t}})\big|_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}=\frac{-2\tau}{(1+\tau)^{2}}\cdot\frac{1}{K}\sum_{1\leq i\leq K}\big(r(x,\mathcal{T}_{i})-\overline{r}(x)\big)\,\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\sum_{\ell}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a^{\ell}_{i}|c^{\ell}_{i})\Big|_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\widehat{L}(\bm{\theta};x,\pi_{\bm{\theta}_{t}})\big|_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}=\frac{-2\tau}{(1+\tau)^{2}}\cdot\frac{1}{K}\sum_{1\leq i\leq K}\big(r(x,\mathcal{T}_{i})-\overline{r}(x)\big)\,\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\sum_{\ell}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a^{\ell}_{i}|c^{\ell}_{i})\Big|_{\bm{\theta}_{t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This motivates the following policy update step:</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g\big(\bm{\theta};x,\{\mathcal{T}_{i},r_{i}\}_{1\leq i\leq K}\big)=\frac{2\tau}{(1+\tau)^{2}}\cdot\frac{1}{K}\sum_{1\leq i\leq K}\big(r(x,\mathcal{T}_{i})-\overline{r}(x)\big)\,\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\sum_{1\leq\ell\leq|\mathcal{T}_{i}|}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a^{\ell}_{i}|c^{\ell}_{i})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\big(\bm{\theta};x,\{\mathcal{T}_{i},r_{i}\}_{1\leq i\leq K}\big)=\frac{2\tau}{(1+\tau)^{2}}\cdot\frac{1}{K}\sum_{1\leq i\leq K}\big(r(x,\mathcal{T}_{i})-\overline{r}(x)\big)\,\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\sum_{1\leq\ell\leq|\mathcal{T}_{i}|}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(a^{\ell}_{i}|c^{\ell}_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">which concludes our derivation of group-relative REINFORCE in multi-step RL settings.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Implementation details and additional experiments</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We implement all algorithms with the Trinity-RFT framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pan et al., 2025</a>]</cite>,
and run experiments on NVIDIA L20, H20, and A800 GPUs.
See Tables <a href="#A2.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ B.2 Understanding the synchronization parameters ‣ Appendix B Implementation details and additional experiments ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#A2.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ B.2 Understanding the synchronization parameters ‣ Appendix B Implementation details and additional experiments ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> for detailed configurations of our experiments.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Dataset details</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide additional descriptions of the datasets used in our experiments:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GSM8k <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al., 2021</a>]</cite> is a widely used benchmark with 8.5k grade-school math word problems, designed to test arithmetic reasoning and step-by-step problem solving.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">MATH <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks et al., 2021</a>]</cite> covers algebra, geometry, probability, and number theory, containing 12.5k examples in total (7.5k for training and 5k for testing); it demands advanced symbolic reasoning beyond GSM8k.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Guru <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cheng et al., 2025</a>]</cite> is a multi-domain reasoning dataset with 91.9k examples spanning math, code, science, logic, simulation, and tabular tasks; we use its math subset (around 54k samples), which introduces diverse problem formats for evaluating transfer of reasoning strategies.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">ToolACE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025a</a>]</cite> is a multilingual benchmark with around 11k synthetic samples designed to evaluate LLMs’ ability to solve tasks by selecting and invoking external tools via strict JSON-formatted function calls; we use a 5k single-turn subset in our experiments.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Understanding the synchronization parameters</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We parameterize rollout-training scheduling by two configuration parameters in Trinity-RFT:
the synchronization interval (<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sync_interval</span>) and synchronization offset (<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sync_offset</span>).
Their meanings are visualized in Figure <a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Experimental setup. ‣ 4 Rethinking the rationales behind recent RL algorithms ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and explained in the following.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The parameter <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sync_interval</span> specifies the number of generated rollout batches (which equals the number of gradient steps for training the policy model) between two consecutive executions of model weight synchronization.
When <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sync_interval</span> <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the rollout and policy models synchronize after each gradient step with one batch of samples,
yielding a strictly on-policy process (if we ignore the issue of precision mismatch between rollout and training engines <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yao et al., 2025</a>]</cite>).
When <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sync_interval</span> <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sync_interval</span> rollout batches are generated with stale model weights before synchronization,
which accelerates the overall RL process through pipeline parallelism but incurs off-policyness.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The parameter <span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sync_offset</span> specifies the lag between the generation and consumption of each batch.
More specifically, <span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sync_offset</span> batches are generated and saved to the buffer before training is launched,
which is also useful for reducing pipeline bubbles and improving hardware utilization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Noukhovitch et al., 2025</a>]</cite>.
In some of our experiments, we deliberately set <span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sync_offset</span> to a large value,
in order to simulate a scenario where reward signals from the environment are lagged.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In general, with <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\texttt{sync\_interval},\texttt{sync\_offset})=(m,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">sync_interval</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">sync_offset</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\texttt{sync\_interval},\texttt{sync\_offset})=(m,n)</annotation></semantics></math>, the off-policyness of a consumed batch with zero-index id <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to its temporal distance from the most recent synchronized policy is <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(l\bmod m)+n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>mod</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(l\bmod m)+n</annotation></semantics></math>. For example, <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(4,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(4,0)</annotation></semantics></math> yields off-policyness <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{0,1,2,3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{0,1,2,3}</annotation></semantics></math> within each interval, while <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,4)</annotation></semantics></math> yields a constant off-policyness of <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="A2.T1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Default hyperparameters. Deviations from defaults are noted in figure captions.
</span></figcaption>
