<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span><span id="A2.SS3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC</span> with different clipping mechanisms</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In addition to one-side clipping investigated in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Rethinking the rationales behind recent RL algorithms ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>,
here we compare additional clipping mechanisms for the <span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC</span> series,
to understand how the geometry of clipping — asymmetric vs. symmetric bounds and the presence of a zero-gradient band —
affects the learning process.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-TwoSide-IS</span>/<span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">NoIS</span>.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We replace the mask <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in <span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-OneSide-IS</span>/<span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">NoIS</span> in Eq. (<a href="#S4.E8" title="In 4.1 Demystifying myths about GRPO ‣ 4 Rethinking the rationales behind recent RL algorithms ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) with a two-side mask<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
                
                
                
              It turns out that <span id="footnote3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-TwoSide-NoIS</span> resembles the sPPO algorithm proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vaswani et al. [2022]</a></cite>, though derived with different rationales.
</span></span></span>:</p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{M}_{i}^{t}=\mathbbm{1}\Big(1-\epsilon_{\textsf{low}}\leq\frac{\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}{\pi_{\textsf{old}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}\leq 1+\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">low</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">high</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{M}_{i}^{t}=\mathbbm{1}\Big(1-\epsilon_{\textsf{low}}\leq\frac{\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}{\pi_{\textsf{old}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}\leq 1+\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Two-side clipping imposes weaker regularization than one-side clipping does with the same clipping parameter <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon_{\textsf{low}},\epsilon_{\textsf{high}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">low</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">high</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon_{\textsf{low}},\epsilon_{\textsf{high}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
This can potentially improve training efficiency, but might also be risky when the probability ratio <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\bm{\theta}}/\pi_{\textsf{old}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">old</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\bm{\theta}}/\pi_{\textsf{old}}</annotation></semantics></math> goes far off.
To compensate for this, we design <span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-Ring</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-Ring</span>.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In addition to the inner band <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\epsilon_{\textsf{low}},1+\epsilon_{\textsf{high}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">low</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">high</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\epsilon_{\textsf{low}},1+\epsilon_{\textsf{high}})</annotation></semantics></math> as in Eq. (<a href="#A2.E18" title="In REC-TwoSide-IS/NoIS. ‣ B.3 REC with different clipping mechanisms ‣ Appendix B Implementation details and additional experiments ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>),
we further specify outer safety margins <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\textsf{low}}^{\prime}\!\geq\!\epsilon_{\textsf{low}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">low</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≥</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">low</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\textsf{low}}^{\prime}\!\geq\!\epsilon_{\textsf{low}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}^{\prime}\!\geq\!\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">high</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≥</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">high</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}^{\prime}\!\geq\!\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The <span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-Ring</span> mask is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{M}_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{M}_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbbm{1}\Big(1-\epsilon_{\textsf{low}}\leq\frac{\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}{\pi_{\textsf{old}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}\leq 1+\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">low</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">high</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbbm{1}\Big(1-\epsilon_{\textsf{low}}\leq\frac{\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}{\pi_{\textsf{old}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}\leq 1+\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\mathbbm{1}\Big(A_{i}&gt;0\text{ and }\frac{\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}{\pi_{\textsf{old}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}\leq 1-\epsilon_{\textsf{low}}^{\prime}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">low</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\mathbbm{1}\Big(A_{i}&gt;0\text{ and }\frac{\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}{\pi_{\textsf{old}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}\leq 1-\epsilon_{\textsf{low}}^{\prime}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\mathbbm{1}\Big(A_{i}&lt;0\text{ and }\frac{\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}{\pi_{\textsf{old}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}\geq 1+\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}^{\prime}\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">high</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\mathbbm{1}\Big(A_{i}&lt;0\text{ and }\frac{\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}{\pi_{\textsf{old}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}\geq 1+\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}^{\prime}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A comparison of the clipping mechanisms are visualized in Figure <a href="#A2.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ REC-Ring. ‣ B.3 REC with different clipping mechanisms ‣ Appendix B Implementation details and additional experiments ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.
Note that <span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-OneSide</span> and <span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-TwoSide</span> can be regarded as special cases of <span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-Ring</span>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.24203v1/rec-force.svg" id="A2.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/95;" width="476" height="95"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A2.F8.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">A visualization of activated gradient for various <span id="A2.F8.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC</span> algorithms.
Here, <math id="A2.F8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> represents the advantage of a specific token, and an arrow pointing to the right and annotated with “<math id="A2.F8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>” means there is activated gradient that incentivizes increasing <math id="A2.F8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\bm{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\bm{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> when the token advantage is positive and the probability ratio <math id="A2.F8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\bm{\theta}}/\pi_{\textsf{old}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">old</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\bm{\theta}}/\pi_{\textsf{old}}</annotation></semantics></math> lies in the corresponding interval.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Experiments.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare the following algorithms:
REINFORCE, GRPO, <span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-TwoSide-IS</span>,
<span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-TwoSide-NoIS</span>, and <span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-Ring-NoIS</span>.
Clipping parameters are set to <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon_{\text{low}},\epsilon_{\text{high}})=(0.2,0.2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>low</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>high</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon_{\text{low}},\epsilon_{\text{high}})=(0.2,0.2)</annotation></semantics></math>,
and for <span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-Ring</span> we additionally set <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon_{\textsf{low}}^{\prime},\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}^{\prime})=(0.6,2.0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">low</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">high</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon_{\textsf{low}}^{\prime},\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}^{\prime})=(0.6,2.0)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F9" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.24203v1/rec_kl_cf.svg" id="A2.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:405/422;" width="405" height="422"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="A2.F9.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of <span id="A2.F9.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC</span> variants on GSM8K with Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct under different off-policy settings. Evaluation accuracy, training reward, KL divergence (with respect to the initial model) and clipping fraction are reported. Training reward curves are smoothed with a running-average window of size 3.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A2.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ Experiments. ‣ B.3 REC with different clipping mechanisms ‣ Appendix B Implementation details and additional experiments ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> presents the empirical results.
We observe that for <span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-TwoSide</span>, importance sampling is non-essential in all three settings, akin to the case of <span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-OneSide</span>.
In addition, <span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-TwoSide</span> methods demonstrate fast policy improvement at the beginning but tend to collapse later on,
whereas <span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-Ring</span> achieves a better balance of convergence speed and stability.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Ablation: the impact of learning rates</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that in Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Demystifying myths about GRPO ‣ 4 Rethinking the rationales behind recent RL algorithms ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>,
we have demonstrated empirically the advantages of enlarging the clipping parameters <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\textsf{low}},\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">low</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">high</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\textsf{low}},\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-OneSide-NoIS</span>.
One might wonder if the relatively weak performance of GRPO or <span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-OneSide</span> with conventional <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\textsf{low}}=\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">low</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">high</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\textsf{low}}=\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math> is genuinely rooted in the clipping mechanism itself, or simply due to the choice of a small learning rate.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To answer this, we enhance the experiment of Figure <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Ablation study with the REC series. ‣ 4.1 Demystifying myths about GRPO ‣ 4 Rethinking the rationales behind recent RL algorithms ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> by sweeping learning rates over <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{1\!\times\!10^{-5},2\!\times\!10^{-6},5\!\times\!10^{-6}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mpadded style="width:0.108em;" width="0.108em"><mo>,</mo></mpadded><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mpadded style="width:0.108em;" width="0.108em"><mo>,</mo></mpadded><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1\!\times\!10^{-5},2\!\times\!10^{-6},5\!\times\!10^{-6}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The results are illustrated in Figure <a href="#A2.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ B.4 Ablation: the impact of learning rates ‣ Appendix B Implementation details and additional experiments ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>,
which confirm that simply increasing the learning rate cannot bridge the performance gap between GRPO with <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\textsf{low}}=\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">low</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">high</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\textsf{low}}=\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math>
and <span id="A2.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-OneSide-NoIS</span> with <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\textsf{low}}=0.6,\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}=2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">low</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">high</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\textsf{low}}=0.6,\epsilon_{\textsf{high}}=2.0</annotation></semantics></math>.
This shows that relaxing the clipping range acts as a genuine improvement of regularization, rather than merely mimicking a larger learning rate.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F10" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.24203v1/ring_lr.svg" id="A2.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:405/159;" width="405" height="159"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>: </span><span id="A2.F10.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of GRPO and <span id="A2.F10.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-OneSide-NoIS</span> on GSM8K with Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct.
Evaluation accuracy (left) and training reward (right) are reported for varying learning rates.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.5 </span>Experiments for OPMD and AsymRE</h3>

<div id="A2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A2.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ B.5 Experiments for OPMD and AsymRE ‣ Appendix B Implementation details and additional experiments ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> presents empirical results for OPMD and AsymRE in various off-policy settings.
It is worth noting that, while the analysis and experiments in their original papers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kimi-Team, 2025b</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Arnal et al., 2025</a>]</cite> focus on a setting that is effectively the same as our <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{sync\_interval}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">sync_interval</mtext><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{sync\_interval}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> setting,
our analysis and experiments have also validated their efficacy in <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{sync\_offset}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">sync_offset</mtext><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{sync\_offset}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> scenarios.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F11" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.24203v1/rep.svg" id="A2.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:405/201;" width="405" height="201"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F11.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>: </span><span id="A2.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Empirical results for OPMD and AsymRE (cf. Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Understanding Kimi’s OPMD and Meta’s AsymRE ‣ 4 Rethinking the rationales behind recent RL algorithms ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>) on GSM8K with Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct under various off-policy settings.
The regularization coefficient for OPMD and the baseline shift for AsymRE are both <math id="A2.F11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Training reward curves are smoothed with a running-average window of size 3.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Summary: a unified view of various algorithms</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For convenient reference, Table <a href="#A3.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Appendix C Summary: a unified view of various algorithms ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> summarizes the algorithms investigated in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Rethinking the rationales behind recent RL algorithms ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.T3" class="ltx_table ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:197.7pt;height:569.7pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><div class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="width:569.7pt;transform:translate(-186.0pt,-186.0pt) rotate(-90deg) ;"><figure>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="A3.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">A summary of algorithms investigated in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Rethinking the rationales behind recent RL algorithms ‣ Group-Relative REINFORCE Is Secretly an Off-Policy Algorithm:Demystifying Some Myths About GRPO and Its Friends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
</span></figcaption>
<table id="A3.T3.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T3.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T3.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Augmentation</span></td>
<td id="A3.T3.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T3.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm</span></td>
<td id="A3.T3.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T3.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gradient / Loss</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T3.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" rowspan="3"><span id="A3.T3.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Regularize by clipping</span></td>
<td id="A3.T3.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">GRPO</td>
<td id="A3.T3.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A3.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{g}=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i}\sum_{t}\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})\cdot A_{i}\frac{\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}{\pi_{\textsf{old}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}M_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{g}=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i}\sum_{t}\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})\cdot A_{i}\frac{\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}{\pi_{\textsf{old}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}M_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T3.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T3.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-OneSide-IS</span></td>
<td id="A3.T3.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A3.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{g}=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i}\sum_{t}\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})\cdot(r_{i}-\overline{r})\frac{\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}{\pi_{\textsf{old}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}M_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{g}=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i}\sum_{t}\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})\cdot(r_{i}-\overline{r})\frac{\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}{\pi_{\textsf{old}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})}M_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T3.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T3.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">REC-OneSide-NoIS</span></td>
<td id="A3.T3.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A3.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{g}=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i}\sum_{t}\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})\cdot(r_{i}-\overline{r})M_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{g}=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i}\sum_{t}\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}^{t}\,|\,x,y_{i}^{&lt;t})\cdot(r_{i}-\overline{r})M_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T3.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" rowspan="2"><span id="A3.T3.5.5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Add regularization loss</span></td>
<td id="A3.T3.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">OPMD</td>
<td id="A3.T3.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A3.T3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{L}=-\tfrac{1}{K}\!\sum_{i}(r_{i}-\overline{r})\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}|x)+\tfrac{\tau}{2K}\!\sum_{i}(\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}|x)-\log\pi_{\textsf{old}}(y_{i}|x))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">old</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{L}=-\tfrac{1}{K}\!\sum_{i}(r_{i}-\overline{r})\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}|x)+\tfrac{\tau}{2K}\!\sum_{i}(\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}|x)-\log\pi_{\textsf{old}}(y_{i}|x))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T3.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.5.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">AsymRE</td>
<td id="A3.T3.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A3.T3.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{L}=-\tfrac{1}{K}\!\sum_{i}(r_{i}-\overline{r})\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}|x)-\tfrac{\tau}{K}\!\sum_{i}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{L}=-\tfrac{1}{K}\!\sum_{i}(r_{i}-\overline{r})\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}|x)-\tfrac{\tau}{K}\!\sum_{i}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T3.5.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.5.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" rowspan="3"><span id="A3.T3.5.7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Reweight data</span></td>
<td id="A3.T3.5.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Pairwise-weighted REINFORCE</td>
<td id="A3.T3.5.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A3.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{g}=\tfrac{1}{K}\!\sum_{i}\Big(\sum_{j}w_{i,j}\Big)\Big(r_{i}-\tfrac{\sum_{j}w_{i,j}r_{j}}{\sum_{j}w_{i,j}}\Big)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{g}=\tfrac{1}{K}\!\sum_{i}\Big(\sum_{j}w_{i,j}\Big)\Big(r_{i}-\tfrac{\sum_{j}w_{i,j}r_{j}}{\sum_{j}w_{i,j}}\Big)\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T3.5.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.5.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">RED-Drop</td>
<td id="A3.T3.5.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A3.T3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{g}=\tfrac{1}{|S|}\!\sum_{i\in S}(r_{i}-\overline{r}_{S})\,\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{g}=\tfrac{1}{|S|}\!\sum_{i\in S}(r_{i}-\overline{r}_{S})\,\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(y_{i}|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T3.5.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.5.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">RED-Weight</td>
